Third-party material
--------------------

The programs that Agent Software Testing measures are not part of this repository. Their source
archives are fetched from the upstream locations named in programs/<id>/program.json and
verified against the SHA-256 recorded there. Each program keeps its own licence:

  bc           GPL-3.0-or-later
  Confetti     MIT
  diffutils    GPL-3.0-or-later
  coreutils    GPL-3.0-or-later   (du, ls)
  gawk         GPL-3.0-or-later
  Gcal         GPL-3.0-or-later
  grep         GPL-3.0-or-later
  gzip         GPL-3.0-or-later
  jq           MIT, with separately licensed bundled components
  Krep         BSD-2-Clause
  libmatheval  GPL-3.0-or-later
  LibYAML      MIT
  vorbis-tools GPL-2.0-or-later   (oggenc); its sanitiser build also fetches libogg
               and libvorbis (BSD-3-Clause)
  sed          GPL-3.0-or-later
  WOFF2        MIT                (with Brotli, MIT, fetched for the build)
  Expat        MIT                (xmlwf)
  xorriso      GPL-3.0-or-later

programs/jq/compat/jq-single-process.c is a small shim written for these builds. It is part
of this repository and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Three build inputs (two patches for Krep and the standard-input driver for libmatheval) were
written by the authors of ConcoLLMic and published in their artifact repository. They are
included below environment/third_party/concollmic/ with the licences that apply to them: the
ConcoLLMic dual licence (the GNU General Public License, version 3, for non-commercial
purposes; the text is in COPYING there) and, for the Krep patches, the Krep licence
(BSD-2-Clause). These files are not covered by the Apache License, Version 2.0 of the rest of
this repository. The build script checks their pinned SHA-256 values before it uses them. See
environment/third_party/concollmic/README.md and environment/README.md.

environment/Dockerfile installs Ubuntu packages (GCC, LLVM/Clang, lcov and others) under
their own licences. No image is distributed by this repository.
